//RS /// D-LIT-DOT1=B (ratified 2026-08-20): named struct construction `Type{ field: val }`.
//RS /// Inferred form (type from context): `{ field: val }` — no type name.
//RS /// The retired dotted forms (`.{…}`, `Type.{…}`) are compile errors (E0320).
//RS /// `jet fmt` still rewrites them. D-UITREE1 (ratified 2026-06-30): the same
//RS /// sigil also constructs a named-payload enum variant — `.Variant{ field: val }`
//RS /// / `Type.Variant{ field: val }` (S30 multi-field variants). No new token;
//RS /// `enum_lit_named_fields` in `Parser/Expressions.rs` parses `{` immediately
//RS /// after a leading-dot variant name.
//RS /// D-LIT-DOT1=B amends D-DOTCTOR3: the same `Type{ body }` head is universal —
//RS /// scalars (`U8{ 250 }`), lists (`[U8]{ 1, 2 }`), fixed arrays (`[U8#3]{ … }`),
//RS /// maps (`[String:Int]{}`), and one-expression assertions (`Int{ fetch_rows() }`).
//RS /// Body elaborates against the head; it never converts. Amends D-EMPTYLIT1:
//RS /// `[T]{}` is the explicit empty; bare `[]` stays contextual. No new token.
//RS pub const OP_NAMED_CTOR: &str = "{";
//RS 
//RS /// D-VARIADIC1 (ratified 2026-06-27): spread/rest sigil — `name: ...T` variadic
//RS /// parameters (last position only), `f(...xs)` call spread, `[...a, x, ...b]` list spread.
//RS pub const SIGIL_SPREAD: &str = "...";
