//RS /// S76 (ratified 2026-06-16): the fixed-size separator in `[T#N]` type
//RS /// position, e.g. `[Int#3]`. Amended by VERSION-# (2026-06-16): `#` also
//RS /// introduces pinned version numbers in package references (`pkg#1.2.0`).
//RS /// Same token, two contexts: `[T#N]` is the type-level size form; `name#ver`
//RS /// is the package version-pin form. No dedicated two-character token in either
//RS /// case — the parser resolves by position.
//RS ///
//RS /// `#` has a third job outside a type: the applied-rule prefix at a
//RS /// declaration/statement/expression target (D-VERDICT-732-1,
//RS /// `RULE_PREFIX`/`MARKER_PREFIX`). D-ONCE-HASH1=B keeps all three jobs on
//RS /// one token, disambiguated only by parser position.
//RS pub const TYPE_FIXED_SIZE_SEP: &str = "#";
