//RS /// three reads that reach the carrier's facts.
//RS ///
//RS /// `.or_err("why")` lifts a clean absence into a failure — the payload rides
//RS /// through untouched and only the report changes. `.partial()` reads the
//RS /// payload a failure kept and `.notes()` reads what it had to say. Both live on
//RS /// the outcome value: an error type opts in by carrying them on its report
//RS /// under the field names below. Writing a note as a `?` hop travels with the
